<wpt lat="37.1918" lon="-89.03754"><name>3-fer US-4572 + US-3791 + US-3793</name><cmt>Guide pin: Riverbank area (approximate)</cmt><desc>US-4572 Lewis and Clark National Historic Trail + US-3791 Trail of Tears National Historic Trail + US-3793 Ballard Wildlife Management Area. Riverbank area (approximate). Pin is on the river side of the park in our map data, not checked against the water line. Walk to the water and set up inside the park within 100 ft of the water. Ohio River: the Lewis &amp; Clark route and the Trail of Tears Water Route. The trail here is the river itself: you must be on public land inside the park AND within 100 ft of the water. The riverbank pin is approximate and has not been checked against the actual water line, so some spots may be farther than 100 ft from the river. Possible only: do your own research. GPS pins are guides only: they get you to the area of a possible 3-fer, not to a confirmed spot. Confirm on the ground that you are inside every park and within 100 ft of the trail or water. Planning tool only: do your own research.</desc><sym>Flag, Blue</sym></wpt>
