<wpt lat="36.49934" lon="-88.0556"><name>3-fer US-3791 + US-0703 + US-3790</name><cmt>Guide pin: Kentucky Lake shore area (approximate)</cmt><desc>US-3791 Trail of Tears National Historic Trail + US-0703 Fort Donelson National Battlefield + US-3790 Fort Heiman National Battlefield. Kentucky Lake shore area (approximate). Pin is on the water side of the park in our map data, not checked against the water line. Walk to the water and set up inside the park within 100 ft of it. Trail of Tears Water Route: the Tennessee River (Kentucky Lake). The trail here is the river itself, so set up on public land inside the park AND within 100 ft of the water. Kentucky Lake is the dammed Tennessee River; the NPS route line follows the old river channel out in the lake, so this is a looser fit than an Ohio River bank. Fort Heiman is a unit of Fort Donelson National Battlefield, so the same land counts for both. The pin is approximate and was not checked against the water line. Possible only: do your own research. GPS pins are guides only: they get you to the area of a possible 3-fer, not to a confirmed spot. Confirm on the ground that you are inside every park and within 100 ft of the trail or water. Planning tool only: do your own research.</desc><sym>Flag, Blue</sym></wpt>
